A||||3||Gokart||New Bosch Platinum+4.......tried yet?
Z||000000||Gokart||08-28-99||09:29 AM||||I feel like I lost a little bit of power over the last month so being on vacation this week I think I'll change my plugs. I bought Bosch's new platinum+4. They are making some outstanding claims (like spitfire did years ago!)Has anyone tried these yet? I'm going to put them in soon and I'll let you know what I think.
Z||000001||Bruce||08-28-99||11:09 AM||||I tried the splitfire plugs on my other car and didn't notice any difference, except that one of the electrodes broke off afte a few thousand miles. I replaced them with Bosch platinum (not the 4+) and have had no problems. I've read claims on either side of the 4+4, so let us know how yours work.
Z||000002||Cooter||08-28-99||04:37 PM||||When I bought my 4cyl fiero, I went ahead and tuned it up the first day I got it with new cap, rotor, filters etc... Since I only had to buy four plugs, I bought the Bosche 4's. I cant say if they make any difference or not because I really did not drive the car enough before to notice any difference. If nothing else- when I hooked the MSD and blaster coil up and watched the fire show at the end of the platinum 4- it looked cool.
Z||000003||Gokart||08-28-99||08:21 PM||||I put them in today and it did restore the power I lost. Runs and idles very smooth. I won't say they gave me MORE power like the thread topic a few months back, but I'll just say I'm happy with the she's running! Parts guy said they will last for 60,000 miles, if so that will make the $35.00 expense worth it.
